**KUDIX PLATFORM — BACKEND DEVELOPMENT REQUIREMENTS**

Hello, I want to explain how the KUDIX platform should function from the backend. Please read through the requirements carefully so that the backend will connect properly with the existing frontend pages, especially the user dashboard and admin dashboard.

KUDIX is a gaming and rewards platform that includes games, social tasks, daily streaks, Watch & Earn, referrals, and other earning features. The backend should make these features functional, configurable, and manageable from the admin dashboard.

### 1. REGISTRATION AND ₦20,000 WELCOME GAMING CREDIT

When a new user registers successfully, the system should automatically credit the user's account with ₦20,000 as a welcome gaming balance.

Important rules:
- The ₦20,000 is strictly for playing games on the platform.
- It is not withdrawable.
- It must not be included in the user's actual earnings or withdrawable balance.
- The gaming balance must be separated from referral rewards, game winnings, and other earnings.
- The user must refer at least three people before becoming eligible to play games.
- The system must automatically check the user's referral count before allowing access to the games.
- Once the user meets the referral requirement, the gaming section should become accessible.

Please implement separate wallet records for promotional gaming credit, actual earnings, referral rewards, and withdrawal requests so that the balances cannot be confused.

### 2. GAME EARNING STRUCTURE

The platform should support a configurable gaming reward structure.

The proposed payout structure is:

- ₦1,000 stake = ₦10,000 payout.
- ₦2,000 stake = ₦20,000 payout.

The administrator should be able to configure the available stake amounts and their corresponding payouts from the admin dashboard.

The backend must validate every stake, game result, and payout. All transactions should be recorded, and the system should prevent duplicate payouts or unauthorized balance changes.

**Important:** Please confirm whether the stated payout amounts represent total returns, including the stake, or profit in addition to the original stake. This distinction must be reflected correctly in the backend calculations.

### 3. GAME MANAGEMENT AND ADMIN CONTROL

The administrator should have complete control over the configurable aspects of the gaming system through the admin dashboard.

The admin should be able to:
- Create, edit, activate, deactivate, and manage games.
- Configure available stake amounts and corresponding payouts.
- Configure game rounds, schedules, and closing times.
- Set the correct results for each game round before the results are revealed.
- Publish the official results to users.
- View participating users, stakes, results, and transaction records.
- View game histories and payout records.
- Enable or disable individual games when necessary.

**Example: Colour Prediction Game**

Suppose the platform has a colour prediction game featuring red, black, and yellow.

The administrator should be able to configure the available colours, establish the official result for a round, and publish that result through the platform.

If game signals or results are announced through a public Telegram channel, the backend should support an appropriate integration or publishing workflow.

The game interface must display the official result consistently with the backend record.

For fairness and accountability, the system should record when each result is created, who configured it, and when it was published. Results should be locked against ordinary edits after the relevant betting round closes, with any authorized correction logged.

### 4. ADMIN DASHBOARD POP-UP MANAGEMENT

The pop-ups that appear on the user dashboard should be controlled from the admin dashboard.

The administrator should be able to:
- Create new pop-ups.
- Edit existing pop-ups.
- Set the title, message, image, and button text.
- Configure the destination of any button.
- Choose when a pop-up should appear.
- Set its start and end dates.
- Enable or disable a pop-up.
- Control whether it appears to all users or a specific eligible group.

Changes made through the admin dashboard should reflect on the user dashboard without requiring manual edits to the frontend code.

### 5. REFERRAL SYSTEM

KUDIX should have a functional referral system.

**Referral reward: ₦1,000 per qualified referral.**

Requirements:
- Every user should have a unique referral code or referral link.
- The system should identify which user referred a new registration.
- Each qualified referral should earn the referring user ₦1,000.
- The reward should be recorded in the user's referral earnings.
- The admin should be able to view referral records and reward transactions.
- Users should be able to see their total referrals, successful referrals, and referral earnings.
- The system must prevent duplicate rewards for the same referral.
- The backend should enforce the three-referral requirement before enabling game access.

Please ensure that a referral is counted only according to the platform's defined qualification rules, rather than simply trusting a registration counter.

### 6. DAILY STREAK SYSTEM

The daily streak feature should reward users for maintaining eligible daily activity.

Requirements:
- A user must refer at least two people before becoming eligible for the streak feature.
- The system should track daily participation and consecutive days.
- Rewards should be calculated and credited according to the configured streak rules.
- The administrator should be able to configure streak requirements, reward amounts, streak duration, and other applicable settings.
- The admin should be able to activate or deactivate the streak feature.
- The system should keep a record of each user's streak history and rewards.

Please review the existing `manage-streak` page and implement the backend according to its available controls and intended functionality.

### 7. BOOST EARNINGS

Please inspect the existing Boost Earn feature and determine how it is intended to work from the current frontend.

The backend should support configurable boost options, eligibility requirements, reward values, activation periods, and other settings relevant to the feature.

The administrator should be able to manage the feature from the admin dashboard.

Before implementing the final earning calculations, please confirm the intended Boost Earn rules so that they match the existing interface and platform requirements.

### 8. WATCH & EARN

The Watch & Earn feature should be managed entirely from the admin dashboard.

The administrator should be able to:
- Add videos.
- Edit video information.
- Upload videos or configure supported video links.
- Set the reward for each video.
- Activate or deactivate videos.
- Set viewing requirements.
- View which users have completed eligible videos.
- View reward and completion records.

On the user dashboard, users should be able to view available videos and see the reward attached to each eligible video.

Rewards should only be credited after the backend verifies that the user's viewing requirements have been satisfied. The system should prevent users from repeatedly claiming the same reward for a single video unless repeat rewards are explicitly enabled.

### 9. LEVEL-UP SYSTEM AND WITHDRAWAL ELIGIBILITY

The Level Up feature should operate through backend rules controlled by the administrator.

I do not want the Level Up requirements or internal eligibility rules displayed prominently on the user dashboard by default.

The administrator should be able to:
- Enable or disable the Level Up system.
- Configure the requirements for eligibility.
- Control when withdrawal eligibility becomes available.
- Review the relevant user records.
- Determine when the withdrawal section should become available according to the configured rules.

When the administrator enables the applicable withdrawal feature, the frontend should display the appropriate withdrawal interface.

Please implement this as a configurable eligibility system rather than hardcoding the requirements into the frontend.

Any withdrawal requirements that affect users' access to their earned funds should be clearly disclosed before users earn or deposit money. The backend should enforce the configured rules consistently.

### 10. WITHDRAWAL MANAGEMENT

The withdrawal system should be manageable through the admin dashboard.

The administrator should be able to configure:
- Minimum withdrawal amount.
- Maximum withdrawal amount, where applicable.
- Available withdrawal methods.
- Applicable fees.
- Withdrawal availability.
- Processing rules.
- Other relevant withdrawal settings.

The user dashboard should allow eligible users to submit withdrawal requests and view their withdrawal history.

The admin dashboard should allow authorized administrators to:
- View pending withdrawal requests.
- Review the user's available withdrawable balance.
- Approve or reject requests with an appropriate reason.
- Mark approved withdrawals as paid only after the payment has been verified.
- View completed, pending, rejected, and failed withdrawals.
- Review the transaction history associated with each withdrawal.

The backend must prevent users from withdrawing promotional gaming credits or other balances that are not eligible for withdrawal.

Every withdrawal status change must be recorded. Balance deductions and payment records must remain consistent, and duplicate processing must be prevented.

### 11. SUPPORT TELEGRAM INTEGRATION

The platform should provide a way for users to access the official KUDIX support Telegram channel or support account.

The administrator should be able to configure the Telegram support destination through the admin dashboard.

When the administrator updates the support Telegram details, the correct destination should appear on the user dashboard or relevant support section.

If a Telegram bot or automated messaging integration is required, please implement it through the appropriate Telegram API and secure backend configuration.

### 12. USER EARNINGS AND TRANSACTION HISTORY

The user dashboard should display accurate financial records.

Users should be able to see their:
- Promotional gaming balance.
- Actual game winnings.
- Referral rewards.
- Streak rewards.
- Watch & Earn rewards.
- Other eligible earnings.
- Total withdrawable balance.
- Pending withdrawal amount.
- Completed withdrawals.
- Relevant transaction history.

Each transaction should include an appropriate description, amount, date, status, and transaction reference.

The backend must calculate balances from verified transactions rather than relying on values supplied by the frontend.

### 13. TOP EARNERS LEADERBOARD

The user dashboard should maintain a Top Earners section.

This section should display users with the highest qualifying earnings according to the platform's configured rules.

The backend should:
- Calculate rankings from verified earning records.
- Update the leaderboard when qualifying transactions are recorded.
- Display the appropriate user information, such as username, rank, and qualifying earnings.
- Exclude promotional gaming credits from actual earnings.
- Avoid counting pending, rejected, or reversed transactions as completed earnings.
- Prevent duplicate transactions from inflating a user's ranking.

Please make sure the leaderboard uses actual backend data rather than hardcoded names or sample statistics.

### 14. COMPLETE ADMIN CONTROL

The admin dashboard should serve as the central management system for the platform.

The administrator should be able to configure the relevant settings for:
- Games and game results.
- Stake amounts and payout structures.
- Promotional gaming credits.
- Referral rewards and referral requirements.
- Daily streaks.
- Boost Earn.
- Watch & Earn videos and rewards.
- Pop-ups and dashboard announcements.
- Level Up eligibility.
- Withdrawal settings.
- Telegram support details.
- User accounts and activity records.
- Transaction histories.
- Leaderboard rules.

Where these controls already exist in the frontend, connect them to the backend instead of redesigning the interface unnecessarily.

Changes should be saved persistently in the database and applied to the relevant user-facing pages.

### 15. DATABASE, SECURITY, AND TRANSACTION RECORDS

Please ensure that the backend is built with reliable database structures and secure transaction processing.

Requirements:
- Store user accounts and referral relationships.
- Maintain separate records for each balance category.
- Store game rounds, stakes, results, and payouts.
- Store streak participation and rewards.
- Store Watch & Earn completion records.
- Store referral rewards and qualification status.
- Store withdrawal requests and payment statuses.
- Store administrator configuration changes.
- Record important administrative actions.
- Protect administrative endpoints against unauthorized access.
- Validate requests on the server.
- Prevent duplicate transactions and reward claims.
- Use appropriate database transactions when updating balances.
- Keep an auditable record of financial changes.

All critical actions must be processed and validated by the backend. The frontend should not be able to grant itself credits, change game results, or approve its own withdrawals.

### 16. CONNECT THE EXISTING FRONTEND

Please review the existing KUDIX frontend files before building the backend.

The goal is to make the current pages functional without unnecessarily changing their existing design.

In particular:
- Connect the user dashboard to actual user data.
- Connect `admin-dashboard.html` to the administrative settings and controls.
- Connect the existing game pages to the game engine and transaction records.
- Connect the streak management page to the streak backend.
- Connect the Watch & Earn interface to the video and reward system.
- Connect the withdrawal interface to the withdrawal backend.
- Connect all relevant forms, buttons, tables, and settings to the appropriate APIs.

Please do not use fake statistics, sample users, simulated earnings, or placeholder transactions as if they were real platform data.

### 17. FINAL EXPECTATION

I want KUDIX to operate as a properly connected platform, not just a frontend with buttons that appear to work.

The backend should manage the actual business logic, database records, user balances, eligibility requirements, rewards, game results, administrative controls, and withdrawal processing.

Please review the existing files, identify the backend requirements for each page, and let me know which parts are already implemented and which still need to be built.

Before finalizing the implementation, please confirm the game payout calculations, the exact Boost Earn rules, the withdrawal eligibility requirements, and the intended game-result workflow.

The final system should be secure, maintainable, and ready for proper testing before going live.